        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-06T22:30:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Filesystems, including f2fs, can have multiple block devices.  This new code is only using the filesystem\u0027s \"main\" block device, which isn\u0027t necessarily where all the encrypted files are.  If the semantics you\u0027re defining for wrapped keys is that they are potentially different for different disks, or that some disks might support them while others don\u0027t, you probably want to enforce that they are only used on single-block-device filesystems.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 546,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 551,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "d40bf3e0ff5b6ec42df22078de23352ab765e53f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
